#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128914 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5165085e-ffa9-533a-ab7c-c03304fc1489" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Level Surface of a Function"}] :question/id #uuid "2f8542a8-1e9e-56f8-9eae-e5b4fb592d4e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5965" :question/problem "Find the family of surfaces that describe the level surfaces of the function $f(x,y, z) = \\ln(x^2 + 2y^2 - z^2)$." :question/worked-solution "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x, y, z) &= c \\\\\n\\ln (x^{2} + 2y^{2} - z^{2}) &= c \\\\\nx^{2} + 2y^{2} - z^{2} &= e^{c} \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{e^{c}} + \\frac{2y^{2}}{e^{c}} - \\frac{z^{2}}{e^{c}} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of hyperboloids of one sheet:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{e^c} + \\dfrac{y^2}{e^c/2} - \\dfrac{z^2}{e^c} = 1, \\qquad c \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128915 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77be6032-ec22-5561-94c2-be289e343142" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Level Surface of a Function Passing Through a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "6a7316fa-77fe-584f-bd92-a37521371482" :question/math-academy-id "e-5966" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z) = \\sin{xyz}$ that passes through the point $P\\left(\\pi,1,\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f\\left(\\pi,1,\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)&= \\sin \\left(\\pi\\cdot 1 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right) = \\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)} = 1 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = c\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c = 1$. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x, y, z) &= c \\\\\n\\sin xyz &= 1 \\\\\nxyz &= \\frac{π}{2} + 2πk\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is any integer.\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point\n\n$$\nP\\left(\\pi,1,\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)\n$$\n\nis the surface\n\n$$\nxyz= \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + 2\\pi k\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is any integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128916 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5e0a37b-23ad-5e79-a175-378b88640ba4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Level Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "397d8dee-c35f-5908-baa6-002e09dab477" :question/math-academy-id "e-5967" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y,z) = x^2+4y^2-z$, find the equation of the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z) = c\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c = 0$. So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x, y, z) &= c \\\\\nx^{2} + 4y^{2} - z &= 0 \\\\\nz &= x^{2} + 4y^{2} \\\\\nz &= x^{2} + \\frac{y^{2}}{1/4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface for $c=0$ is the elliptic paraboloid\n\n$$\nz = x^2+\\dfrac{y^2}{{1/4}}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77be6032-ec22-5561-94c2-be289e343142" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Level Surface of a Function Passing Through a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83f9679a-77aa-5779-8751-da471ca7f744" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 2y + 3z - \\ln 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127053} {:answer/id #uuid "1c0f75cc-9015-553b-8e5d-2cd1d25e55e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + y^{2} + z^{2} = (\\ln 3)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127054} {:answer/id #uuid "54b483e6-fc19-5cb7-a406-35b4f3bd48f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + y^{2} + z^{2} = 3^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127055} {:answer/id #uuid "62d88181-cccd-51ca-a3bb-f3dbc441a9de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 2y + 3z - 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127056} {:answer/id #uuid "743e62ee-63f0-5e96-837b-48fcba2d0924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 2y + 3z + \\ln 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62d88181-cccd-51ca-a3bb-f3dbc441a9de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x + 2y + 3z - 3 = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127056} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc679e0-a7d6-5713-be8e-680452069640" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127052}] :question/id #uuid "96466546-d66d-5bfb-9320-7db7a3c30bde" :question/math-academy-id "q-36986" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x, y, z) = \\ln (x + 2y + 3z)$ that passes through the point $P(1, 1, 0)$."}]}
